R (https://www.r-project.org) is distributed under the GNU General Public
License, version 2 or later (R 4.6.2: doc/COPYRIGHTS). Its sources are used
here in exactly one way: the released program is run as an oracle, and what it
prints is recorded in testdata/golden. The following rules follow from the
licensing decision of 2026-11-01 (BSD-3-Clause for the whole repository; the R
code of base R is rewritten, never copied, never downloaded at run time):

1. No file of the R source tree (C, Fortran, R, Rd, tests, .Rout.save) is
   committed here, and no code is translated from one.
2. Golden files hold the answers of R 4.6.2 to inputs written in this
   repository (testdata/snippets.R, testdata/values.R); they are outputs of the
   program, not R's own test data.
3. The format of R's serialization (package rds) is implemented from the
   section "Serialization Formats" of the R Internals manual and from the bytes
   the reference R 4.6.2 writes; the numeric codes of the pseudo-types the
   manual does not number (references, special environments, ALTREP) were
   observed on that output. No text of the manual is copied.
4. Contributors do not read src/main, src/nmath or the R code of the base
   packages while writing their Go or R counterparts (CONTRIBUTING.md).

5. Clean-room process. cmd/cleanroom scores every file of eval/baselib
   against the R code of R 4.6.2 (token k-gram winnowing, exact and with
   identifiers normalised, plus the longest common token run); it reads R's
   sources at check time only, from a tree the caller provides, and reports
   file:line references, never R's text. The gate (thresholds measured on
   independent code, README "Clean-room process") runs as a test and in the CI
   oracle lane, against the tarball pinned by SHA-256. Run:
   RGO_RSOURCE=<R-4.6.2 tree> go run ./cmd/cleanroom check

Test tooling downloads, in CI and on a developer's machine, the conda-forge
build of R 4.6.2 as an unmodified program. It is not part of this repository
and is not redistributed by it.

The Go module dependencies (github.com/spf13/cobra, github.com/spf13/pflag,
github.com/inconshreveable/mousetrap) are Apache-2.0 / BSD-3-Clause licensed;
see their repositories.
